==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|el}} {{term|ἴσος|tr=isos|lang=el||equal}} + {{term|μορφή|tr=morphe|lang=el||shape}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{biology}} the [[similarity]] in [[form]] of [[organism]]s of different [[ancestry]]
# {{algebra}} A [[bijection]] ''f'' such that both ''f'' and its [[inverse function|inverse]] ''f''<sup>&nbsp;&minus;1</sup> are [[homomorphism]]s, that is, structure-preserving mappings.
# {{chemistry}} the similarity in the [[crystal]] structures of similar [[chemical]] [[compound]]s
# {{sociology}} the similarity in the structure or [[processes]] of different [[organization]]s
# {{computer science}} a [[one-to-one]] [[correspondence]] between all the [[element]]s of two [[set]]s, e.g. the [[instance]]s of two [[class]]es, or the [[record]]s in two [[dataset]]s

